+++ b/source/provenance/provenance-notes.xml
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ was updated or created.
 When a Provenance resource is used to record the removal of a resource, the Provenance.target references the removed resource, and the Provenance.entity indicates the removed resource as well. For example, <a href="provenance-example-delete.html">example delete</a> shows the use of Provenance to record the deletion of a resource. 
 If versioning is supported, 
 the version that was removed is referenced in Provenance.target; if versioning is not supported then 
-Provenance.target contains the non-version reference. 
+Provenance.target contains the non-version reference. This is enforced by the <code>prov-5</code> invariant.
 </p>
 <p>
 When replacing a Resource, and it is important to track which Resource replaces the removed Resource. One Provenance Resource SHOULD be used to indicate a replace. For a replace the Provenance.target points at both the removed resource and the new resource, and the Provenance.entity indicates the removed resource. For example, <a href="provenance-example-correction-replacement.html">example correction with replacement</a> shows the use of Provenance to record the replacement of an historic immunization with a new immunization resource.
